.TH LLITE.PCC_ASYNC_THRESHOLD 4 2026-11-10 "Lustre" "Lustre Kernel Interfaces"
.SH NAME
llite.pcc_async_threshold \- file size threshold for background PCC attach
.SH SYNOPSIS
.SY
.RI "lctl get_param llite." FSNAME *.pcc_async_threshold
.SY
.RI "lctl set_param llite." FSNAME *.pcc_async_threshold= SIZE
.YS
.SS PROPERTIES
.TP
.B Access Permissions
.br
.BR 644 " | " -rw-r--r--
.TP
.B Scope
.br
Per local filesystem mountpoint.
.TP
.B Config
.br
.B pcc_async_threshold
is always present for client mountpoints.
.TP
.B Default
.br
.RB pcc_async_threshold= 268435456 " (256MiB)"
.TP
.B Valid Range
.br
.RB pcc_async_threshold= 0
.br
.RB pcc_async_threshold= 18446744073709551615 " (16EiB)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B pcc_async_threshold
parameter controls how a file is copied into a PCC-RO cache when it is
attached automatically by an
.B O_RDONLY
.BR open (2)
that matches a PCC backend with PCC-RO enabled.
Files of at least
.I SIZE
bytes are copied in the background by a dedicated kernel thread,
smaller files are copied before
.BR open (2)
returns and are attached to the file for later use.
File descriptors opened before the background copy finishes use the
uncached OST I/O path until they are closed, while later opens use the
PCC copy.
This may duplicate some reads to the Lustre OSTs initially, but reduces
the initial read latency when an application first accesses a large file.
The threshold does not apply to files attached with
.BR lfs-pcc-attach (1),
which are always copied synchronously.
.PP
If
.BR llite.pcc_attach_thread_max (4)
background attaches are already running, the file is copied
synchronously regardless of its size.
.PP
The
.I SIZE
parameter is specified in bytes by default, but may specify unit suffixes
.B KMGTP
for values in
.BR K ibibytes,
.BR M ebibytes,
.BR G ibibytes,
.BR T ebibytes,
and
.BR P ebibytes
respectively.
.SH MODULES
This parameter is in the following modules:
.EX
.B llite.*.pcc_async_threshold
.EE
.SH EXAMPLES
Always use a background data copy to import files into the PCC cache:
.EX
.RB "mgs# " "lctl set_param -P llite.testfs-*.pcc_async_threshold=0"
.EE
.SH AVAILABILITY
The
.B llite.pcc_async_threshold
parameter is part of the
.BR lustre (7)
filesystem package since release 2.16.0.
.\" Added in commit v2_15_64-10-g5be466e873
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR lfs-pcc-attach (1),
.BR open (2),
.BR read (2),
.BR llite.pcc_attach_thread_max (4),
.BR lctl-get_param (8),
.BR lctl-set_param (8)
